The attached image, corresponding to Figure 10 in the PDF, illustrates the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site 24 hours post-intramuscular injection in skeletal muscle. The top row shows fluorescently labeled Nano-11 (red) and various inflammatory cells (green), including Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages, MHCII+ cells, neutrophils (1A8), and F4/80+ macrophages, recruited to the site after injection with Nano-11-adsorbed ovalbumin. Intracellular Nano-11 within Mac-2+ and MHCII+ cells indicates efficient phagocytosis by these antigen-presenting cells. The bottom row displays the nuclei (blue) and muscle fibers, providing structural context. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to recruit immune cells and facilitate antigen uptake in vivo.